# Rust / Tauri build output. Two things are deliberately NOT ignored:
#   · src-tauri/icons — generated once by tools/make-icon.js, and the build
#     needs them, so a fresh clone must not have to run Node first.
#   · Cargo.lock — this is an application, not a library. Pinning the exact
#     dependency graph is what makes a rebuild months from now produce the same
#     agent, which matters more here than usual: this one terminates processes.
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/
